    "stem": "Pranav studies a number grid where each entry increases by $1$ across a row and by $10$ down a column. He claims that in any $2\\times 2$ block the two diagonal sums are equal, for every such block.\n\nWhich two claims correctly prove that the relation always holds?",
    "item_type": "mcq",
    "options": {
      "A": "Check four sample blocks and stop once those samples match.",
      "B": "Let the top-left entry be $n$. The block is $n$, $n+1$, $n+10$, $n+11$; both diagonals equal $2n+11$.",
      "C": "The same letter-number offsets show the other diagonal is also $n+(n+11)=2n+11$, so the sums match for every $n$.",
      "D": "Equal diagonal sums are what create the $1$-across and $10$-down grid steps."
    },
